Z||000000||Standard||02-07-2000||01:36 AM||||Got myself an 86.5 GT 5spd!  I love the v6!  I could just sit behind it and listen to the exhaust all day.. if any of you were reading my "need advice" thread you know what it looks like, but I'll post 'em again<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PlanteGT.jpg">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PlanteGT2.jpg">   <BR>ended up paying him $1100.  Starts up and runs fine, gonna need a battery soon.  Handles better than my 84.  More bumb steer, but i'm going from 185/80's on the 84 to 195/60 in front and 205/60 on the rear.  Needs front exh. manifold.  No cat(and not gonna get one.. exhaust note is sweet, and smog checks in mn stopped last novemeber!!)  Body's pretty rough, needs paint but a buff and polish would probably shine it up ok.  Gonna give it the usual tune.. plugs, wires, oil change, that stuff.  Can't wait till I get tags and insurance on this thing!!  I'm spoiled for life, never gonna go back to 4 cyl!<P>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 02-07-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 02-08-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||sdm1964||02-07-2000||06:20 AM||||Congrats!!! You will love the v-6, I have an 85 GT, I want an aero coupe next.||||reg||7
